-- title:
--   Igusa branch through an end of the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hqM'`, `hℓ12`, `hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`) admitting a complex reading: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$ (`hι`).
--
--   *Level and function field.* The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is required (`hH₁`) to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((t))$ (Laurent series over $L$) is required (`hK`) to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise extension $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   *Base ring.* $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring which is an $L$-subring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`), with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), with uniformiser $\varpi$ (`hϖ`: $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$), and with a tame constant $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfying $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q \cdot (\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`). Moreover $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$.
--
--   *Chart and supersingular point.* $j$ is a nonzero element of $K$ whose Laurent series is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the $q$-expansion $t^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral } j\text{-numerator})$) under coefficient extension (`hj`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, $j_C \in C$ for $j$ itself, and $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and the morphism `ιFin` from $X_{\mathrm{fin}} := \operatorname{Spec} C$ into $X$. The ideal $y \subset C$ is maximal (`hy`), contains the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_C)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   *The Drinfeld-chart witness hypothesis `hArig`.* For every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `ιFin`$(y') = z$ whose prime is supersingular in the above sense, there exist: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f\,u\big)$, subject to seven clauses. Writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the completion map, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY} : C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the germ map along `ιFin` at $y'$, these are: (i) $e(\mathrm{toC}(\text{germ of } a)) = \mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma a))$ for $a \in A$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (the condition that $\tau$ realises on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ the substitution by the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, read through embeddings $L \to \mathbb{C}$ normalised by $\zeta \mapsto e^{2\pi i /q}$), $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if in addition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, then $\tau(a) - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are $\theta \in \operatorname{Aut}(S)$, $c \in W$ and $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta \circ e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} = e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} \circ \tau$ on $C$, with $\theta$ fixing the constants $\mathrm{mkS}(C(w))$, with $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_j)) \equiv \mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\big)$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, with $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and with $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, each containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$ and an element $\mathrm{mkS}(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (vi) for $P$ a prime of $S$ not containing both $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$ and an element $\mathrm{mkS}(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a \in C$: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $j_E - a_0 \in y'$ (where $j_E$ denotes that element of $C$), an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in W$, at least one of which is a unit, with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(j_E - a_0))) = \mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   *The chosen point and an explicit witness there.* A point $z$ of $X$ together with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $z$ (`hy'`) with supersingular prime (`hss'`), and $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`: $y'$ has underlying ideal $y$). Further, an explicit witness $W_1$ (a complete discrete valuation ring), $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ with $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for this data at this $z$ and $y'$, precisely the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   *The centre ideal and the blown-up chart.* The ideal $J \subset C$ is required (`hJ`) to be the infimum of all ideals of the form $\big(\tau|_C\big)^{-1}\Big(\big(e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}\big)^{-1}\big(\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\,\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\,\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)\big)\Big)$, taken over $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $L$-automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ with `IsLevelAutAt`$\dots\gamma^{-1}\dots$ preserving $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is required (`hB`) to be obtained by adjoining to $C$ all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$, that is $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   *Properties of $B$ and of a distinguished valuation ring $W$.* $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypotheses `hR1` ($C \subseteq B$, and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$), `hR2` ($A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension $\le 1$), `hR3` (five clauses: $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b \in C$, $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$) and `hEQ` (four clauses, summarised here: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k[X_0,X_1]/(\text{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ with kernel the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W$, through an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c)$ in the kernel `hSubgroup q` of $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)c^{q+1}$ acting by `hAction`, with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; such $\tau$ preserve $B$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit by $\tau(\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B)$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; an element of $B$ carried into $\mathfrak{m}_W$ by all such $\tau$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$) are all assumed.
--
--   *Further data.* `hjK` and `hjC`: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$. An integer $m \ge 1$ (`hm1`) with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t \cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hmt`).
--
--   *Ends.* `ends` is a finite set of subrings of $K$ characterised (`hends`) by: $O \in$ `ends` if and only if there is $a \in J$, nonzero in $K$, such that, setting $B_a := C\big[\{x \in K : x a \in J\}\big]$ as an $A$-subalgebra of $K$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ equal to the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (that is, $f \in O$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$), with no element of $y$ becoming a unit in $O$, and with $B \not\subseteq O$.
--
--   *The prescribed end and its crossing data.* $O \in$ `ends` (`hOmem`) satisfies $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), contains $C$ (`hCO`) and $\varpi$ (`hϖO`). There are $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, and an isomorphism $\iota$ of the $\mathfrak{m}_O$-adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat{A}\,[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \varpi^m)$ over the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic completion $\widehat{A}$, together with units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y = \varpi^m u$ (`hcxy`), $\iota$ sends the image of each $a \in A$ lying in $O$ to the constant $a$ (`hιc`), $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ (`hιx`) and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$ (`hιy`), while $c_y \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcyW`) and $c_x \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcxW`).
--
--   *Conclusion.* Under these hypotheses there exists a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K$ with all of the following properties: $O \subseteq W_x$; every element of $C$ lies in $W_x$; for $x \in L$, the image of $x$ lies in $W_x$ if and only if $x$ lies in the image of $A$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring; $\varpi$ lies in $W_x$ and $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ is generated by $\varpi$; there exists $t \in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $A$, if $p(t)$ (coefficients mapped into $L$) lies in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; the same transcendence statement holds with [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in place of $t$: if $p$ evaluated at that element lies in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$, then all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; $c_x \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ whenever $c_x \in W_x$; $c_y \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ whenever $c_y \in W_x$; every $b \in C$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ lies in $y$; there exists $b \in y$ which does not lie in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$; and for every $O' \in$ `ends` with $O' \ne O$ there exists $f \in O'$ with $f \notin W_x$.
--
--   This is the step, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model, that attaches to a prescribed end of the blown-up chart the valuation ring of an Igusa branch: a discrete valuation subring of the modular function field, unramified over the base uniformiser, whose residue data are transcendental over the residue field of $A$, whose centre on the $j$-finite chart is strictly smaller than the supersingular maximal ideal $y$, and which separates the given end from all other ends. It is used by the companion statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_igusaValuationSubring_translateSep_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_igusaValuationSubring_translateSep_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), and it is assembled from the crossing-model branch construction, the transcendence statement for the $j$-value, and the separation statement for ends.
